OldNetTexts: {
	OldNetHarvest: +{0} Mold Shards (uninscribed)
	OldNetNodeHint: Recover data
	OldNetTerminalHint: Log out and inscribe your haul
	OldNetSettleDone: Inscribed {0} Mold Shards — link severed safely
	OldNetSettleEmpty: Link severed safely — nothing recovered this dive
	OldNetEjectRam: RAM depleted — link burned out, uninscribed haul lost
	OldNetEjectDeath: Construct collapse — link burned out, uninscribed haul lost
	OldNetLedgerFull: Ledger full — hit a relay or log out first
	OldNetEncryptHint: Channel decryption (stand still ~3s, loud)
	OldNetEventHint: Pull the breaker: unseal the vaults, wake the whole net
	OldNetEventPulled: Seals released — purge wave inbound
	OldNetRelayHint: Relay uplink: inscribe current ledger (the uplink makes noise)
	OldNetRelayDone: Inscribed {0} Mold Shards — link holds
	OldNetRelayEmpty: Ledger empty, nothing to uplink
	OldNetEnterHint: Jack into the OldNet (dive beyond the Blackwall)
	OldNetEnterConfirm: Link warmed up — interact again to dive beyond the wall
	OldNetEnterSPOnly: Diving is single-player only
	OldNetDiveCharge: Hold the descent — crossing the wall
	OldNetBandFoot: Wallfoot Belt // FOOTHOLD
	OldNetBandRuin: Ruinfield // RUINFIELD
	OldNetBandFade: Signal Decay Zone // SIGNAL DECAY
	GuideNoiseTitle: The Noise Meter
	GuideNoiseBody: Bottom-left is your noise meter — moving, firing and cracking all light you up. The four ticks are four threat tiers; past T2, something comes from the wall. Stand still and the noise cools off on its own.
	GuideLedgerTitle: The Uninscribed Ledger
	GuideLedgerBody: Shards you harvest go into the ledger first (the LEDGER readout). Death or RAM burnout voids all of it — only what you inscribe is truly yours. The ledger has a capacity and refuses overflow.
	GuideNodesTitle: Node Grades
	GuideNodesBody: Cyan nodes harvest on right-click. Amber encrypted nodes need ~3s of channeling — loud, but worth triple. The red event breaker unseals every vault on the map, and brings the purge wave with it.
	GuideRelayTitle: Relay vs Logout
	GuideRelayBody: The amber column is a relay — inscribe on the spot and keep diving, but the uplink is loud. The mint column is the logout terminal — inscribe and sever safely. Greed or retreat, that is the only question here.
	GuideDrainTitle: Distance Drain
	GuideDrainBody: The farther from the wall, the pricier the RAM drain — the DEPTH readout shows your current cost per second. Burning out means ejection, so budget the trip home in advance.
	GuideSkip: Got it
	EntrustTitle: Dive Beyond the Wall
	EntrustSummary: The OldNet's entrance is the crashed sky-island above spawn: climb the anchor rope hanging down to the ground, and the cyan-lit pillar in the mid-hull is the access terminal. Right-click it to warm the link, then right-click again within 5 seconds to dive in (single-player only). Inside, right-click cyan nodes to recover mold shards; they land in your ledger first. To keep them, return to the foot of the Blackwall and right-click the mint column to log out. One safe logout completes this commission. RAM burnout or death on the way voids everything uninscribed.
	EntrustCategory: Deep-Dive Archaeology
	TrackerOverworld: Reach the mid-hull of the crashed pod above spawn; right-click the cyan terminal twice
	TrackerDive: Return to the Blackwall's foot; right-click the mint column to log out safely
	OldNetSignRuin: Ruinfield. Prime harvest grounds — encrypted nodes from here on. Mind your exit before you channel.
	OldNetSignFade: Signal Decay Zone. The drain climbs steeply past this point — the link won't hold long. Proceed at your own risk.
	OldNetEchoHint: Echo node — only tangible during time-freeze (zero noise, double yield)
	OldNetEchoFizzle: The echo is too faint — only tangible in frozen time
	OldNetCacheHint: Deep-dive cache — pry it open for a sealed module (loudly)
	OldNetTripwireHint: Raster tripwire: crossing the lit beam reports your position; hold right-click to cut it
	OldNetTripwireCut: Cut. This route is quiet now
	OldNetMineHint: Sentry mine: rush in and it detonates; approach slowly and hold right-click to defuse
	OldNetMineDefused: Defused. Nothing heard it
	OldNetMineScream: The sentry mine screams; your position is broadcast
	OldNetMineDeath: "{0} set off a sentry mine"
	OldNetBulkheadWarn: High-noise signature detected; shaft bulkheads pre-tensioning
	OldNetBulkheadShut: Shafts sealed. Quiet down and wait for reopen, or force one open with a pressure breaker
	OldNetBulkheadReopen: Noise has settled; shaft bulkheads reopening
	OldNetBreakerHint: Emergency breaker: pull to open the gate for 8 seconds, at the cost of more noise
	OldNetBreakerPulled: Pressure vented; gate open for 8 seconds
	OldNetSignCheckpoint: Quarantine Checkpoint K-3. Signals east of this line are unsanitized; no live protocols may pass. This checkpoint fell on Night 771.
	TaggerAttached: Signal tagged. While it lives, your noise will not decay on its own.
	TracerHowlWarn: The hound is broadcasting your position. Interrupt it.
	TracerConfused: Path crossed. It has lost the scent.
	WardenDispatch: Reclamation protocol authorized. An executor is peeling off the blackwall.
	WardenSlain: Executor archived. The whole net falls silent for you, 60 seconds.
	WardenGraceHud: Silence grace
	OldNetDockHint: Right-click to expand: +8 ledger slots this dive, +15 noise
	OldNetDockDone: Ledger +8 slots
	OldNetColdHint: Right-click to extract: costs 2 RAM, silent
	OldNetColdNoRam: Not enough RAM — extraction needs 2
	OldNetEscrowHint: Right-click to insure: 30% of the ledger as premium, +10 noise on uplink. Pays out the rest on burnout or death; no refund on safe logout
	OldNetEscrowEmpty: Ledger empty — nothing to insure
	OldNetEscrowTooThin: Ledger too thin — the premium would eat everything, nothing to insure
	OldNetEscrowSigned: Insured {0} shards, premium {1}
	OldNetEscrowPayout: Insurance paid out {0} Mold Shards
	OldNetVaultHint: Right-click to breach: costs 3 RAM, +2 noise per second while open. Every stage raises the stakes; miss and the pot burns
	OldNetVaultNoRam: Not enough RAM — breaching needs 3
	OldNetVaultLocked: Console already running
	OldNetVaultPayout: Pot banked — {0} shards (uninscribed)
	VaultTitle: Cipher Matrix
	VaultGuide: Click or press jump as the needle sweeps the lit arc. Getting hit or stepping away mid-spin counts as a miss
	VaultStage: Stage {0} / 5
	VaultPot: Pot: shards ×{0}
	VaultPotModule: Sealed modules ×{0}
	VaultPotChip: RAM capacity chip ×1
	VaultLedgerRoom: Ledger room: {0}
	VaultCashOut: Cash out
	VaultContinue: Next stage
	VaultBust: Bust — pot cleared
	VaultCounterHack: Console counter-hack: injection inbound
	VaultDiscard: Ledger full — {0} shards discarded
	OldNetEncryptFadeHint: Channel decryption: the mad zone's locks bite back — completing one always draws a hunt
	OldNetAftershockWarn: Residual exposure — the echo is tracing back
	OldNetAftershockHit: Traceback complete. They are coming
	OldNetDragnetWarn: The net is drawing shut — the threat is about to become irreversible // DRAGNET 75%
	OldNetDragnetOn: Dragnet engaged: the purge never lifts, every encrypted lock is offline // DRAGNET
	OldNetHotExtractHint: Link overheated: severing takes 10 seconds at the terminal, and the net will come for you
	OldNetHotExtractStart: Forced severance started — hold the line // SEVERING
	OldNetHotExtractAbort: Severance aborted — the link holds
	OldNetHotExtractTooFar: Too far from the terminal — get closer to sever
}

